    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "db2e5f26_5560ac36",
        "filename": "acme/autocert/autocert.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 96,
      "author": {
        "id": 5065
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-08-17T22:54:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m fine with that too, even though our Cache interface as-is isn\u0027t suitable for pre-populating anything, since it\u0027s so opaque.\n\nBut for performance, no need to check the policy func for a cert we have cached.\n\nAlso, start by documenting what it does (\"controls access\"), not immediately jumping to how it does so (\"is evaluated\").\n\n  // HostPolicy controls which domains the Manager will attempt\n  // to retrieve new certs for. It does not affect cached certs.\n  // If nil, ....\n  // If non-nil, HostPolicy is called before retrieving a new cert.\n  // If it returns an error, XXXX.",
      "parentUuid": "bb944b51_d35c8389",
      "revId": "18b76d22ec7017a2bc21165f67c7c34d14d5cb4b",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "db2e5f26_3512d0b3",
        "filename": "acme/autocert/autocert.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 97,
      "author": {
        "id": 5065
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-08-17T22:54:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Really? So this is a required field and it should be above Cache.\n\nBut this might be an overly-strict policy. I think a better default policy would be to check the machine\u0027s hostname, and/or check that the domain name\u0027s DNS points to this machine\u0027s local IP. Or even allow everything, maybe rate-limited.\n\nI don\u0027t like the idea of this being a required field for most casual users. (but I do think we need some sort of default protection)",
      "revId": "18b76d22ec7017a2bc21165f67c7c34d14d5cb4b",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705",
      "unresolved": false
